          "id": "48d98499-184a-3f11-a486-edd5cd1447a0",
          "content": {
            "id": "48d98499-184a-3f11-a486-edd5cd1447a0",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Ryanair CEO responds to Musk's takeover threat in ongoing spat",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: :: Profanity warning</p><p>:: Ryanair\u2019s Michael O\u2019Leary responds to Elon Musk after ruling out Starlink internet on his aircraft</p><p>:: Dublin, Ireland</p><p>:: January 21, 2026\u00a0\u00a0</p><p>\"Elon Musk apparently took great umbrage and resorted to insulting me on X at the weekend, calling me an idiot. I think yesterday he also rounded on me and called me, I think, a retarded twat. All I would say to Elon Musk is he would have to join the back of a very, very, very, very long queue of people who already think I'm a retarded twat, including my four teenage children.\"</p><p>\"We have been in discussion with Starlink, his satellite system, for about over 12 months now. It is a very good system. [...] The Starlink people believe that 90% of our passengers would happily pay for Wi-Fi access. Our experience sadly tells us we think less than 10% of our passengers pay for this access, and therefore we can't afford to shoulder costs of between 150 and 250 million a year.\"</p><p>\"We noticed he was holding a poll about should he launch a bid for Ryanair. We're a publicly owned company, he's free to do so at any time, but non-European citizens cannot own a majority of European airlines.\"</p><p>Elon Musk on Friday (January 16) called Ryanair CEO Michael O'Leary an \"utter idiot\" who should be fired, escalating a public spat that began after the airline boss ruled out installing Musk's Starlink internet service on Ryanair aircraft.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: :: Profanity warning</p><p>:: Ryanair\u2019s Michael O\u2019Leary responds to Elon Musk after ruling out Starlink internet on his aircraft</p><p>:: Dublin, Ireland</p><p>:: January 21, 2026&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>\"Elon Musk apparently took great umbrage and resorted to insulting me on X at the weekend, calling me an idiot. I think yesterday he also rounded on me and called me, I think, a retarded twat. All I would say to Elon Musk is he would have to join the back of a very, very, very, very long queue of people who already think I'm a retarded twat, including my four teenage children.\"</p><p>\"We have been in discussion with Starlink, his satellite system, for about over 12 months now. It is a very good system. [...] The Starlink people believe that 90% of our passengers would happily pay for Wi-Fi access. Our experience sadly tells us we think less than 10% of our passengers pay for this access, and therefore we can't afford to shoulder costs of between 150 and 250 million a year.\"</p><p>\"We noticed he was holding a poll about should he launch a bid for Ryanair. We're a publicly owned company, he's free to do so at any time, but non-European citizens cannot own a majority of European airlines.\"</p><p>Elon Musk on Friday (January 16) called Ryanair CEO Michael O'Leary an \"utter idiot\" who should be fired, escalating a public spat that began after the airline boss ruled out installing Musk's Starlink internet service on Ryanair aircraft.</p></body>",
